3","Name":"SetConfigurationKeyMultiValue","FullInfo":"Siemens.OpcenterEX.ReferenceData.Configuration_RF.RFModel.Commands.SetConfigurationKeyMultiValue","TypeResolved":"","_project":{"$ref":"12"},"_domain":{"$ref":"592"}}},"FullIdObj":{"$ref":"665"},"Children":[],"Name":"CommandName","ScriptInfo":{"$ref":"589"},"Documentation":{"$id":"666","$type":"DslTerminalNode","Text":"Lets you edit multiple values of configuration key.\r\nThe command performs the following checks and returns an error accordingly:\r\n12300: checks if the Configuration Key Multi Value exists.\r\n14002: checks if Configuration Key has boolean value (True/False).\r\n14003: checks if Configuration Key has numeric value.\r\n14005: checks if Value has 2 decimal places for NId.\r\n14007: checks if Configuration Key Multi Value has a Value.\r\n14008: checks if Guid for NId is valid.\r\n14009: checks if support for securing application data is enabled in User Management Console.\r\n14011: checks if the Value field (marked as Protected) has exceeded maximum length (100).","FullInfo":"Lets you edit multiple values of configuration key.\r\nThe command performs the following checks and returns an error accordingly:\r\n12300: checks if the Configuration Key Multi Value exists.\r\n14002: checks if Configuration Key has boolean value (True/False).\r\n14003: checks if Configuration Key has numeric value.\r\n14005: checks if Value has 2 decimal places for NId.\r\n14007: checks if Configuration Key Multi Value has a Value.\r\n14008: checks if Guid for NId is valid.\r\n14009: checks if support for securing application data is enabled in User Management Console.\r\n14011: checks if the Value field (marked as Protected) has exceeded maximum length (100).","InfoMap":{"$id":"667","FullIdObj":{"$id":"668","$type":"IdentificableText","Name":"Lets you edit multiple values of configuration key.\r\nThe command performs the following checks and returns an error accordingly:\r\n12300: checks if the Configuration Key Multi Value exists.\r\n14002: checks if Configuration Key has boolean value (True/False).\r\n14003: checks if Configuration Key has numeric value.\r\n14005: checks if Value has 2 decimal places for NId.\r\n14007: checks if Configuration Key Multi Value has a Value.\r\n14008: checks if Guid for NId is valid.\r\n14009: checks if support for securing application data is enabled in User Management Console.\r\n14011: checks if the Value field (marked as Protected) has exceeded maximum length (100).","FullInfo":"Lets you edit multiple values of configuration key.\r\nThe command performs the following checks and returns an error accordingly:\r\n12300: checks if the Configuration Key Multi Value exists.\r\n14002: checks if Configuration Key has boolean value (True/False).\r\n14003: checks if Configuration Key has numeric value.\r\n14005: checks if Value has 2 decimal places for NId.\r\n14007: checks if Configuration Key Multi Value has a Value.\r\n14008: checks if Guid for NId is valid.\r\n14009: checks if support for securing application data is enabled in User Management Console.\r\n14011: checks if the Value field (marked as Protected) has exceeded maximum length (100).","TypeResolved":""}},"FullIdObj":{"$ref":"668"},"Children":[],"Name":"Documentation","SystemAnnotations":[],"CustomAnnotations":[],"TagAnnotations":[],"_text":"Lets you edit multiple values of configuration key.\r\nThe command performs the following checks and returns an error accordingly:\r\n12300: checks if the Configuration Key Multi Value exists.\r\n14002: checks if Configuration Key has boolean value (True/False).\r\n14003: checks if Configuration Key has numeric value.\r\n14005: checks if Value has 2 decimal places for NId.\r\n14007: checks if Configuration Key Multi Value has a Value.\r\n14008: checks if Guid for NId is valid.\r\n14009: checks if support for securing application data is enabled in User Management Console.\r\n14011: checks if the Value field (marked as Protected) has exceeded maximum length (