Id is valid.\r\n14009: checks if support for securing application data is enabled in User Management Console.\r\n14011: checks if the Value field (marked as Protected) has exceeded maximum length (100).","FullInfo":"Adds the configuration key.\r\nThe command performs the following checks and returns an error accordingly:\r\n12301: checks if the Configuration Key already exists, using its natural identifier.\r\n14001: checks if Configuration Key has a Value.\r\n14002: checks if Configuration Key has boolean value (True/False).\r\n14003: checks if Configuration Key has numeric value.\r\n14005: checks if Value has 2 decimal places for NId.\r\n14008: checks if Guid for NId is valid.\r\n14009: checks if support for securing application data is enabled in User Management Console.\r\n14011: checks if the Value field (marked as Protected) has exceeded maximum length (100).","InfoMap":{"$id":"812","FullIdObj":{"$id":"813","$type":"IdentificableText","Name":"Adds the configuration key.\r\nThe command performs the following checks and returns an error accordingly:\r\n12301: checks if the Configuration Key already exists, using its natural identifier.\r\n14001: checks if Configuration Key has a Value.\r\n14002: checks if Configuration Key has boolean value (True/False).\r\n14003: checks if Configuration Key has numeric value.\r\n14005: checks if Value has 2 decimal places for NId.\r\n14008: checks if Guid for NId is valid.\r\n14009: checks if support for securing application data is enabled in User Management Console.\r\n14011: checks if the Value field (marked as Protected) has exceeded maximum length (100).","FullInfo":"Adds the configuration key.\r\nThe command performs the following checks and returns an error accordingly:\r\n12301: checks if the Configuration Key already exists, using its natural identifier.\r\n14001: checks if Configuration Key has a Value.\r\n14002: checks if Configuration Key has boolean value (True/False).\r\n14003: checks if Configuration Key has nume